# Commit notes

When the user asks for a **commit message**, **commit note**, or **PR / changelog summary** from current work:

1. **Inspect the tree** — Run `git branch --show-current`, `git status --short`, and staged diffs (`git diff --cached --stat`, `git diff --cached`). Use unstaged or branch-wide diffs only when nothing is staged or the user asks. Base the message only on what is actually changed; do not invent files or behavior.

2. **Scope** — If unrelated changes are mixed (e.g. docs + feature), say so and offer **two commit messages** (split by concern) or one combined message, whichever fits the user’s likely intent.

3. **Branch prefix & title** — Parse the current branch name:
   - **Prefix:** leading ticket segment — `FE-034`, `BE-012`, `FE-BE-034`, etc. (matches `FE-`, `BE-`, or `FE-BE-` followed by digits).
   - **Title:** infer from the remainder of the branch name (slug after the prefix). Convert kebab-case to a readable title in Title Case; expand common abbreviations (`auth`, `api`, `e2e`, `ui`) when helpful. The title should summarize intent, not list files.
   - If the branch has no ticket prefix, use only the inferred title on the first line (no prefix).

4. **Output format** — Reply with **only** the commit message body, ready to paste into the commit message field. No markdown headings, fences, or wrapper text unless the user asks for commentary.

```
{PREFIX}: {Title inferred from branch}

{One short paragraph: what changed and why — complete sentences, plain language.}

- {Imperative bullet: concrete change}
- {Another bullet}
- …
```

**Example** (branch `FE-034-move-community-guidelines-to-settings`):

```
FE-034: Move Community Guidelines to Settings & Privacy > Community & Safety

Relocates Community Guidelines from the profile view into a dedicated
Community & Safety settings page, keeping the profile section cleaner
and grouping safety content with other settings.

- Remove Community Guidelines block from ProfileView
- Add Community & Safety entry to SettingsPrivacy section list
- Create CommunitySafety page at /settings/community-safety with
  guidelines rendered as an accessible list
- Register new route in App.tsx
- Update ARCHITECTURE.md routing docs
- Add/update unit tests for SettingsPrivacy and CommunitySafety
- Add E2E test covering Community & Safety navigation flow
```

5. **Bullets** — One idea per bullet; imperative mood (“Add”, “Remove”, “Update”). Mention areas (`front-end`, `back-end`, tests, config, docs) when relevant. Wrap long bullets at ~72 characters. Skip noise (lockfile-only, formatting-only) unless that is the whole change.

6. **Tone** — Clear, technical prose without filler. Every bullet must map to something in the diff.
